     the same reason: `.shot-light` is only applied when a dark counterpart
     exists, so a project with a single screenshot is never hidden.

     display:none is what keeps this cheap. The hidden variant is lazy, so it
     never intersects the viewport and is never fetched; toggling the theme
     reveals it and only then does it load.
     ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  .shot-dark {
    display: none;
  }

  :root[data-theme='dark'] .shot-light {
